      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-309597",
      ":question/problem": "The function $g$ is defined by $g(x) = ax^{2} + bx + c$, where $a, b$, and $c$ are constants. The graph of $y = g(x)$ in the $xy$-plane passes through the points $(4, 0)$ and $(-2, 0)$. If $a$ is an integer greater than $1$, which of the following could be the value of $a + b$?\n\n1. $-3$\n2. $0$\n3. $3$"
